config WTK_FT8719_E977
	bool "FocalTech FT8719 touch for the MediaTek package (Doogee S88 Pro, from the disassembly)"
	default n
	help
	  FocalTech FT8719 touchscreen of the Doogee S88 Pro, reconstructed by
	  reading the disassembled factory kernel.  The factory config turns it
	  on (CONFIG_WTK_FT8719_E977=y in e977_dg_m13_71_q0.config) and the ALPS
	  tree does not have the symbol: without this entry `olddefconfig`
	  discards the factory config line in silence.

	  THE BATCH IS COMPLETE since 2026-08-22: the factory block has 67
	  functions in SIX translation units, and all 67 are here.

	    focaltech_core.c            unit C  16 fn
	    focaltech_sysfs.c           unit A  22 fn
	    focaltech_flash.c           unit B  17 fn
	    focaltech_ex_mode.c         unit D   3 fn
	    focaltech_i2c.c             unit E   7 fn
	    focaltech_ft8719_upgrade.c  unit F   3 fn (plus the upgrade)

	  64 of the 67 match to the byte with the factory compiler
	  (clang-r353983c).  The three that do not are in focaltech_core.c:
	  tpd_probe, get_module_id and touch_event_handler.

	  THIS TEXT USED TO SAY "THE DRIVER DOES NOT LINK" and listed unit B as
	  missing in full: that was true when it was written and is not any more.
	  The name `focaltech_flash.c` is a declared CHOICE -- FocalTech does not
	  use `pr_debug`, so there are no `_ddebug` descriptors naming its files
	  and the binary does not give the name.
